From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 31 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 13/13] Fix gallery not opening from the capture thumbnail
 (camera freeze)

Bug: tapping the capture thumbnail after taking a photo/video did not
open the Gallery and left the camera preview stuck/unresponsive.

Root cause: patch 0007 ("Change com.android.camera.action.REVIEW to
android.provider.action.REVIEW") changed the outgoing "review" intent
built in the thumbnail-tap handler (GalleryHelper.gotoGallery, called
from the thumbnail click path) to use the action
"android.provider.action.REVIEW" with no package/category set. Our
MIUIGalleryGlobal.apk (com.miui.gallery, the HyperOS Gallery port used
on this device) does not declare any <intent-filter> for that action
-- it only handles "com.miui.camera.action.REVIEW",
"com.miui.camera.action.REVIEWX" and "com.android.camera.action.REVIEW"
(see TranslucentExternalPhotoPageActivity / ExternalPhotoPageActivity
in its manifest). So startActivity() throws
ActivityNotFoundException.

That exception IS caught, but the fallback handler
(GalleryHelper.s(), "review activity not found!") retries with an
explicit setPackage("com.miui.mediaviewer") -- a separate MIUI system
component that is not part of this device's proprietary blobs / is not
installed on this ROM -- so the fallback ALSO throws
ActivityNotFoundException, which is silently swallowed and logged as
"review image fail.".

Before either startActivity() attempt, gotoGallery() already calls
Camera.Co()/pauses the preview to prepare for the transition to the
gallery. Since both startActivity() calls fail and the exception is
swallowed, that preview-pause state is never undone, which is why the
camera appears to hang/freeze after tapping the thumbnail instead of
either opening the gallery or showing an error.

Fix: point the thumbnail-review intent back at
"com.miui.camera.action.REVIEW", which our shipped Gallery build
explicitly declares (routed to the translucent review activity that
matches the camera's transition/lockscreen theming, consistent with
patch 0009 "Force enable StartActivityWhenLocked"). This mirrors the
change into camera version 5.3.001050.2's current (re-obfuscated)
class names: what shipped as l3.smali/a6.smali in older MiuiCamera
builds is now r3.smali/o6.smali in the currently vendored APK, so this
patch targets those files instead of l3.smali/a6.smali directly.

This does not touch patch 0006's "Support third party galleries"
change (the separate general "open Gallery app" intent, matched via
category android.intent.category.APP_GALLERY on the main launcher
activity), which already resolves correctly and is unaffected by this
bug.
---
 smali/com/android/camera/o6.smali | 2 +-
 smali/com/android/camera/r3.smali | 4 ++--
 2 files changed, 3 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/smali/com/android/camera/o6.smali b/smali/com/android/camera/o6.smali
index 0000000..0000000 100644
--- a/smali/com/android/camera/o6.smali
+++ b/smali/com/android/camera/o6.smali
@@ -210,7 +210,7 @@

 .field public static final d1:Ljava/lang/String; = "com.miui.securitycenter.action.INVISIBLE_SETTING"

-.field public static final e:Ljava/lang/String; = "android.provider.action.REVIEW"
+.field public static final e:Ljava/lang/String; = "com.miui.camera.action.REVIEW"

 .field public static final e0:I = 0x8c36

diff --git a/smali/com/android/camera/r3.smali b/smali/com/android/camera/r3.smali
index 0000000..0000000 100644
--- a/smali/com/android/camera/r3.smali
+++ b/smali/com/android/camera/r3.smali
@@ -1107,7 +1107,7 @@

     move-result p0

-    const-string v0, "android.provider.action.REVIEW"
+    const-string v0, "com.miui.camera.action.REVIEW"

     if-eqz p0, :cond_0

@@ -1168,7 +1168,7 @@

     const-string p1, "GalleryHelper"

-    const-string v1, "gotoGallery: android.provider.action.REVIEW"
+    const-string v1, "gotoGallery: com.miui.camera.action.REVIEW"

     invoke-static {p1, v1, p0}, Lcom/android/camera/log/Log;->d(Ljava/lang/String;Ljava/lang/String;[Ljava/lang/Object;)V

